---
<BaseLayout title={`Medicolegal Fundamentals | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="UK medical law principles applied to radiology. Foundational cases, NHS claims data, and landmark historical authorities. Bolam, Bolitho, Montgomery, causation, breach and consent — with radiology application for each.">
<PageHero eyebrow="Medicolegal Fundamentals" title="Medicolegal Fundamentals" description="UK medical law: foundational cases, NHS data, historical authorities and radiology application." heroImage={PAGE_HERO_IMAGES["/medicolegal-fundamentals"]} />

<PageIntro
	eyebrow="Medicolegal law library"
	paragraphs={[
		'The legal half of the resource, kept deliberately short and selective. Each entry states the principle, names the authority, and then says what it means for a radiologist reading a study or writing a report.',
		'It is arranged in four parts: the foundational cases that established the core principles of medical negligence law; the NHS claims data that shows where radiology disputes actually arise; the landmark historical cases that shaped the modern law; and the applied principles — standard of care, consent, causation, interpretation, reporting standards, candour and AI-assisted reporting.',
	]}
	contents={[
		{ href: '#foundational-cases', label: 'Foundational law cases' },
		{ href: '#nhs-data', label: 'NHS claims data' },
		{ href: '#historical-cases', label: 'Important historical cases' },
		{ href: '#standard-of-care', label: 'Standard of care' },
		{ href: '#consent', label: 'Consent' },
		{ href: '#causation', label: 'Causation' },
		{ href: '#interpretation', label: 'Interpretation and breach' },
		{ href: '#reporting-standards', label: 'Reporting standards' },
		{ href: '#candour', label: 'Duty of candour' },
		{ href: '#ai-reporting', label: 'AI-assisted reporting' },
	]}
	audience="Written for radiologists, trust legal teams, solicitors, barristers and expert witnesses."
	reviewed="September 2026"
/>

<div class="container-page space-y-12 band">
	<Figure
			label="Figure 01"
			caption="The four questions a radiological claim resolves into"
